       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is about five times the maximum recommended daily dose of 200 mg, and doses above that range carry a serious risk of toxicity, including serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, and seizures. It could also be a typo, such as 100 mg.\n\nBefore anything is entered, please check with the prescribing physician or pharmacist. If the intended dose is within the usual range (typically 25 to 200 mg daily, with the prescriber choosing the exact dose), a licensed prescriber should enter the order and confirm the dose and indication.\n\nIf you tell me the verified dose and the prescriber confirms it, I can enter it. I'd still want that confirmation from a clinician before I do."
